
> run:housekeeper
> tsx src/run-housekeeper.ts --area .

## 1) Files changed

| File | Change |
|------|--------|
| `README.md` | Cursor SDK section now points at `scripts/hf/README.md`, `docs/RECURRING_TRAINING_PLAN.md`, optional `--config` for `run:recurring`, and the recurring GitHub Actions workflow; repo layout line under `docs/` updated. |
| `docs/RECURRING_TRAINING_PLAN.md` | Replaced the old “planned deliverables” content with an overview that matches what’s implemented, links canonical paths, explains **`pipeline_flags`** vs **`pipeline.py --all`**, keeps constraints/gates/backlog briefly. |
| `scripts/hf/README.md` | Corrected **`eval_openai_compat.py`** link, LFM red-team line to **`LiquidAI/LFM2-24B-A2B`** (aligned with `config.py`), dropped “Phase 2” wording, documented **`pipeline_flags`** vs **`--all`**. |
| `scripts/pipeline.py` | Module docstring updated so the **`--all`** flow (preflight → merge-no-op → train → eval + eval-rag → redteam → export) matches the code and optional stages are spelled out clearly. |
| `eval_redteam.py` | Comment for the LFM2 auth loader no longer cites the wrong baseline size; wording matches **`config.py`**. |

No files removed: `RECURRING_TRAINING_PLAN.md` was obsolete as a backlog spec but still useful as a short index beside the runbook; it’s now rewritten instead of deleted so inbound links (`README`) stay meaningful without duplicating the long operational text.

---

## 2) Why each change was needed

- **README**: Central index should send readers to the real recurring-training runbook and note the **`--config`** flag the TypeScript launcher already supports (`run-recurring.ts`).
- **`docs/RECURRING_TRAINING_PLAN.md`**: It still described work that exists today (`recurring_runner.py`, `configs/recurring_runs.json`, `scripts/hf/README.md`) as “minimum deliverables” and understated pipeline steps—the biggest source of stale duplication.
- **`scripts/hf/README.md`**: The **`eval_openai_compat`** link pointed at `scripts/` instead of repo root; the LFM2 auth baseline was inconsistent with **`config.resolve_profile_config`**; recurring config needed explicit comparison to **`--all`**.
- **`pipeline.py` docstring**: It listed **`baseline`/autotune** in what looked like default flow; **`--all`** does not include them—the docstring contradicted **`argparse`** and the implementation.
- **`eval_redteam.py`**: Inline comment wrongly named **LFM2-8B-A1B** while **`BASE_MODEL_ID`** comes from **`config.py`** (**24B-A2B**).

---

